---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Run the Lab Locally — Hanoi Local Zone Field Notes"
  description="Rehearse all three AWS Hanoi Local Zone scenarios locally with Docker, Toxiproxy, PostgreSQL, and the interactive portal."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Hands-on · No AWS required"
    title="Rehearse the path before paying for it."
    marker="LOCAL_NETWORK_EMULATION"
    lede="The local lab performs real HTTP and PostgreSQL work with configured network effects. It teaches the workflow without claiming to predict AWS performance."
  />

  <section class="section shell quickstart">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Fresh clone</p><h2>Three commands to first light.</h2></div>
      <p>PowerShell 7+, Node.js 22+, Docker Desktop, Git, and Terraform are expected. AWS credentials are not required for local emulation.</p>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Install the workspace</h3><pre><code>npm ci</code></pre></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Check local prerequisites</h3><pre><code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\lab.ps1 doctor</code></pre></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Build and start the lab</h3><pre><code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\lab.ps1 local -Build</code></pre></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell destinations">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Working surfaces</p><h2>Learn, act, then inspect.</h2></div>
      <p>The portal explains the operations. The Mini Order App demonstrates the business behavior.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="destination-grid">
      <article><span>3000</span><h3>Interactive portal</h3><p>Overview, learning, scenarios, setup, infrastructure, benchmarks, operations, and end-to-end demo workspace.</p><code>http://localhost:3000</code></article>
      <article><span>8081</span><h3>Mini Order App</h3><p>Create and inspect synthetic orders while seeing the active endpoint, location, mode, and request timing.</p><code>http://localhost:8081</code></article>
      <article><span>3001</span><h3>Loopback agent</h3><p>Fixed allowlisted actions, CSRF and Origin protection, sanitized SSE logs, and no arbitrary browser shell.</p><code>http://127.0.0.1:3001</code></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell workflow">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Local learning path</p><h2>Follow the same shape as AWS.</h2></div>
      <p>Local mode rehearses the mental model and UI interactions while keeping provenance visibly separate.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="workflow-line" aria-label="Recommended local lab sequence">
      {[
        ["01","Doctor"], ["02","Start"], ["03","Verify"], ["04","Cases 1–3"], ["05","Benchmark"], ["06","Inspect"], ["07","Stop"]
      ].map(([number,label]) => <div><span>{number}</span><strong>{label}</strong></div>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reading-shell caution">
    <p class="eyebrow">Do not cross the evidence streams</p>
    <h2>Emulation explains behavior. It does not forecast AWS.</h2>
    <p>Configured Toxiproxy delay and jitter are teaching inputs. Local output is labelled `LOCAL_NETWORK_EMULATION`; the retained cloud run is `HISTORICAL AWS_REAL`; the current AWS deployment state is `NOT_DEPLOYED`.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .quickstart { padding-top: 0; }
  .quickstart ol { margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); list-style: none; }
  .quickstart li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; min-height: 150px; align-items: center; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .quickstart li > span { color: var(--cyan); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .68rem; }
  .quickstart h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.7rem; }
  pre { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0; padding: 15px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; background: #050810; color: var(--green); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .78rem; }
  .destination-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .destination-grid article { min-height: 330px; padding: 36px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: rgba(12,18,32,.72); }
  .destination-grid span { color: var(--orange); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .destination-grid h3 { margin: 72px 0 14px; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; }
  .destination-grid p { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .destination-grid code { color: var(--cyan); font-size: .7rem; }
  .workflow-line { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(7,1fr); border-block: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .workflow-line div { position: relative; display: grid; min-height: 120px; align-content: center; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 14px; }
  .workflow-line div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .workflow-line span { color: var(--ink-faint); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .62rem; }
  .workflow-line strong { margin-top: 8px; font-size: .78rem; }
  .caution { text-align: center; }
  .caution h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(2.7rem,6vw,5rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .caution p:last-child { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 850px) { .destination-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .workflow-line { overflow-x: auto; grid-template-columns: repeat(7,140px); } }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .quickstart li { grid-template-columns: 42px minmax(0,1fr); } }
</style>
